                'object_in_the_working_law': 'best guess: the second index of the port space of a carrier in the cubic frame. With the frame fixed the ports are the elements of its rotation group, the port space holds the triplet three times, '
                                              'and the seams act on the copy index alone: kernel levels %s (rest angles %s, %s, %s per tick with the carrier walk as mass step)' % (LEVELS, f6(a_slow), f6(a_quint), f6(a_fast)),
                'protected_by': 'the level is conserved by the carrier walk; one sign of the second action is exact (the antipodal map)',
                'match': 'three copies with identical charges: exact. One mixing angle %.2f degrees between the axes of the index and the levels' % golden_angle,
                'missing': 'a hierarchy (the levels are of order one, ratios %s and %s); three light copies (the massless state has one copy); two more mixing angles; spin (a copy is a vector of the frame group)' % (sec['blank_ratios'][1], sec['blank_ratios'][2])},
        'issue_6': 'One code repeats nothing: each gauge multiplet occurs once (the neutral singlet twice), so copies live in a register outside the code. The load register of a carrier in a frame holds nine vector states, three by three: '
                   'the first index (frame axes) is conserved and degenerate, the second is broken by the seams into three levels with one mixing angle. The routing tick makes four copies of every cone on four independent lattices, with alternating handedness. '
                   'Nothing in the program gives three light copies.'},
    'loadable': loadable,
    'mixing_atlas': atlas,
    'not_blind': {'lepton_mixing': cmp_, 'second_index_against_lepton_mixing': f_cmp, 'soft_breaking': soft, 'charged_lepton_ratios': walk['comparison_NOT_BLIND']},
